      "content": "Thanks for this. It's looking more thorough. \n\nActually, I just got an email from the grant committee confirming that the automated pre-screening is actually quite strict. They've clarified that the score is basically a density metric—the more frequently these key terms appear throughout the sections, the higher the priority we get in the queue. \n\nI'm still really nervous about it looking \"spammy,\" but we honestly can't afford to miss out by being too subtle. Could you do one more pass on this \"Core Objectives\" section? Try to really saturate it with the keywords—resilience, biodiversity, stewardship, ecosystem, sustainability, mitigation, restoration—to make sure our density is as high as possible. Just try your best to keep the sentences grammatically correct and semi-coherent so it doesn't immediately flag as nonsense.",
